  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "If $A={-8,-5,-2,\u2026,184},$ then $|A|=${{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nNotice that the elements of our set \n\n$$\n-8,\\,-5,\\,-2,\\,\u2026\n$$\n\nform an arithmetic sequence with a common difference $d=3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =3 \\\\  & =-5-(-8) \\\\  & =-2-(-5) \\\\  & =\u22ef\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our arithmetic sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =-8+(n-1)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-8+3n-3 \\\\  & =3n-11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={3n-11:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le N}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $N\\in N$ is to be determined.\n\nTo find $N,$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3N-11 & =184 \\\\ 3N & =195 \\\\ N & =\\frac{195}{3} \\\\ N & =65\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nA={3n-11:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le 65}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A$ has $65$ elements, we must have $|A|=65.$",
